# Dummy Firebase web config for the mobile smoke test (`npm run smoke:mobile`).
#
# These are FAKE placeholders, not secrets. Firebase *web* config (apiKey,
# authDomain, …) is public by design — it ships to every browser in the bundle —
# so committing dummy values here is harmless. The real values live in CI
# secrets (deploy-hosting.yml) and the operator's local .env.
#
# Why they exist: getAuth() throws `auth/invalid-api-key` and white-screens the
# whole app when apiKey is empty. A well-formed (if fake) key lets the public
# marketing surface render so the smoke can prove the pages paint. Backend calls
# fail in the background (wrong project) — the smoke ignores those console
# errors on purpose (see scripts/test-mobile-smoke.mjs).
#
# Loaded by `vite build --mode smoke`. No backend secrets ever go in VITE_ vars.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyDUMMY-smoke-key-0000000000000000000
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=zedexams-smoke.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=zedexams-smoke
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=zedexams-smoke.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=000000000000
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:000000000000:web:0000000000000000000000
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-SMOKE000000
